{
  "dom_id": "step-q10404",
  "name": "Question 1",
  "problem": "What is the domain of the function  $f(x)=2\\operatorname{cot}\u2061(3x)?$ Assume that $n$ is an integer.",
  "worked_solution": "The domain of $y=\\operatorname{cot}\u2061x$ is given by the expression\n\n$$\nx\\ne n\\pi ,\n$$\n\nwhere $n$ is an integer.\n\nTo find the domain of $2\\operatorname{cot}\u2061(3x),$ we replace the $x$ on the left-hand side of the above with $(3x).$ This gives\n\n$$\n3x\\ne n\\pi .\n$$\n\nSolving for $x,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3x & \\ne n\\pi  \\\\ x & \\ne \\frac{n\\pi }{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the domain of the function is $x\\ne \\frac{n\\pi }{3},$ where $n$ is an integer.",
